fiers of position-effect variegation in the region from 86C to 88B of the Drosophila melanogaster third chromosome.</article-title><source>Mol Gen Genet</source><volume>210</volume><fpage>429</fpage><lpage>436</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3123888</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003864-Reuter2"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reuter</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Szidonya</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1983</year><article-title>Cytogenetic analysis of variegation suppressors and a dominant temperature-sensitive lethal in region 23&#x02013;26 of chromosome 2L in Drosophila melanogaster.</article-title><source>Chromosoma</source><volume>88</volume><fpage>277</fpage><lpage>285</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6418476</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003864-Reuter3"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reuter</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Werner</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Hoffmann</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>1982</year><article-title>Mutants affecting position-effect heterochromatinization in Drosophila melanogaster.</article-title><source>Chromosoma</source><volume>85</volume><fpage>539</fpage><lpage>551</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6813058</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003864-Reuter4"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reuter</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolff</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><year>1981</year><article-title>Isolation of dominant suppressor mutations for position-effect variegation in Drosophila melanogaster.</article-title><source>Mol Gen Genet</source><volume>182</volume><fpage>516</fpage><